From b365a0272921a05fd11f811dec1b95002db1b78f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 10:42:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01268/11171] [conductor] OFF-ARC TRANSFER POWER --
 COLLECT+VALIDATE (operator TOP PRIORITY; G1; THE headline question): poll for
 the backgrounded run launched by exp4044; recompute the 10,000-resample
 TASK-LEVEL bootstrap CI95 for (Arm B demo-fit - Arm A vote) over N>=160 --
 DOES THE CI NOW EXCLUDE ZERO? Also report whether a stronger arm (Arm C
 symbolic-partition / Arm A++ ACES) lifts the delta above naive demo-fit.
 Check the POSITIVE CONTROL (oracle headroom present -> informative;
 oracle~=vote -> ceiling-saturated, uninformative, escalate). Emit the
 verdict: (1) demo-fit CI EXCLUDES 0 -> the shared GAP-4 primitive MEASURABLY
 generalizes to code (the operator's headline); (2) demo-fit CI still touches
 0 but a stronger arm excludes 0 -> the primitive transfers but needs a
 code-specialized discriminator (log GAP-CODE-EXEC-DEMOFIT); (3) all arms
 touch 0 with headroom -> honest small-magnitude transfer; (4) no headroom ->
 uninformative, harder corpus.

Automated research step by research conductor.
Task ID: exp4045-offarc-transfer-power-collect

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
